    "id": "assetDesign",
    "name": "AssetDesign",
    "description": "An Asset Design represents an abstract definition of an asset, generally, when an engineering drawing exists for a particular asset - that would be the \"design\". Generic asset (i.e. non-serialized) can be associated to products, as just an asset design. Asset designs themselves, do not get inventoried, they do not have maintenance performed against them. ",
    "dataModelKindId": "reference"
  },
